From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] supplicant: do not offer SAE on wpa-psk station connections

For key-mgmt=wpa-psk NetworkManager also advertises SAE/FT-SAE so that an
existing WPA2 profile keeps working if the AP is later upgraded to WPA3.
The comment above the test says this must not happen when PMF is disabled,
but the test reads

    (!is_ap || pmf != NM_SETTING_WIRELESS_SECURITY_PMF_DISABLE)

and !is_ap is true for every station, so SAE is offered regardless of the
PMF setting.  Disabling PMF therefore only has an effect in AP mode.

That breaks the AIC8800 on the Radxa ZERO 3W.  It is a fullmac part: its
firmware builds the association request itself and advertises plain
WPA-PSK, while wpa_supplicant puts the full AKM list in EAPOL message 2.
The AP sees the two differ and deauthenticates with reason 17, which
wpa_supplicant reports as "pre-shared key may be incorrect".

Verified on the board: running wpa_supplicant by hand with
key_mgmt=WPA-PSK, or with "WPA-PSK WPA-PSK-SHA256 FT-PSK", associates and
completes the 4-way handshake; adding SAE is what fails.

Offer SAE only in AP mode, where the PMF check works as intended.
---
--- a/src/core/supplicant/nm-supplicant-config.c	2026-11-14 03:03:07.656660100 +0200
+++ b/src/core/supplicant/nm-supplicant-config.c	2026-11-14 03:03:07.859509300 +0200
@@ -1009,10 +1009,10 @@
          * some devices that are not fully compatible with WPA3-Personal
          * transition mode.
          */
-        if (_get_capability(priv, NM_SUPPL_CAP_TYPE_SAE)
+        if (is_ap && _get_capability(priv, NM_SUPPL_CAP_TYPE_SAE)
             && _get_capability(priv, NM_SUPPL_CAP_TYPE_PMF)
             && _get_capability(priv, NM_SUPPL_CAP_TYPE_BIP)
-            && (!is_ap || pmf != NM_SETTING_WIRELESS_SECURITY_PMF_DISABLE)) {
+            && pmf != NM_SETTING_WIRELESS_SECURITY_PMF_DISABLE) {
             g_string_append(key_mgmt_conf, " SAE");
             if (!is_ap && _get_capability(priv, NM_SUPPL_CAP_TYPE_FT))
                 g_string_append(key_mgmt_conf, " FT-SAE");
